# Introducing {{PRODUCT_NAME}}

## Overview

This skill produces consistent, high-quality introduction materials for {{PRODUCT_NAME}} across different scenarios, audiences, and formats.

{{CORE_DESCRIPTION_PARAGRAPH}}

## Workflow

1. Read [references/product-brief.md](references/product-brief.md) first.
2. When a specific output type or audience is requested, read [references/output-recipes.md](references/output-recipes.md).
3. When deeper methodology or strategic framing is needed, read [references/foundational-logic.md](references/foundational-logic.md).
4. When specific product examples or content samples are needed, read [references/materials-guide.md](references/materials-guide.md).
5. When brand assets need to be used, read [references/brand-assets.md](references/brand-assets.md).
6. When visual layout or design direction is needed, read [references/visual-direction.md](references/visual-direction.md).
7. If the user has not specified target audience and output purpose, infer them.
8. Default to the Core Information Order below when organizing content.
9. Adjust information density, tone, and call-to-action per output scenario.

## Core Information Order

Unless the user requests a highly specific output, organize content in this order:

1. What it is
2. What it contains
3. Why it matters today
4. What problem it solves
5. What value it creates for {{TARGET_AUDIENCE}}
6. How it differs from alternatives

